# Backend Standards

Backend work must comply with:

- `specs/README.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-001-security-baseline.md`
- `specs/security/SEC-002-security-testing.md`
- `spec-driven/24-erp-023-backend-core-foundation.md`

SEC-001 defines required protections. SEC-002 defines the evidence required to validate them.

Mandatory backend expectations:

- validate input schemas strictly and reject unexpected fields;
- enforce auth, authorization, role checks and ownership checks server-side;
- prevent IDOR, BOLA and broken function-level authorization;
- use prepared statements or ORM-safe queries only;
- never log secrets, passwords, cookies, tokens or authorization headers;
- enforce strict CORS, content type validation, payload size limits and rate limits;
- add security tests for auth, permissions, tenant isolation, uploads and critical business logic.
